    title: "About Cadre AI",
    content: "## Summary\n\nCadre AI is an AI strategy and implementation consultancy. The firm's positioning is \"from AI confusion to AI confidence\": most companies know they should be using AI but don't have a clear plan, and Cadre acts as an embedded team that finds the highest-value opportunities, implements them, and trains the client's people so the change actually sticks.\n\n## Key facts\n\n- Founded in San Diego, California, in November 2024.\n- Works with businesses ranging from startups to large enterprises, with particular depth in lower middle market private equity–backed companies, professional services firms, and financial services organizations.\n- Official service partner of both OpenAI and Anthropic; also works with Google, Microsoft, AWS, Salesforce, and Snowflake, and can access a broad range of models through OpenRouter.\n- Approach: go department by department inside a client's business, identify the highest-ROI AI opportunities, implement the tools/workflows/agents, then train the team so adoption sticks — rather than handing over a slide deck and walking away.\n- Core belief: companies that treat AI as a scattered set of individual tools (some employees on ChatGPT, others on Claude, no shared strategy) create real risk — wasted spend, inconsistent results, and sensitive data handled inconsistently. Cadre's role is to bring structure and ownership to that.\n- The team includes AI strategists, AI managers, and AI engineers working from a shared framework across engagements.\n\n## If asked something not covered here\n\nQuestions about specific client engagements, financial results, or team headcount are not covered by public information — escalate rather than guess.",
